NPU-side gate (Loom AIE2P array programs): lets an NPU job wait for a flag in memory itself, so a GPU and the NPU can
hand work over without a host relay.
- constrain.core_stream %ch: an external channel on the worker core's own stream port (mov.ss / mov.ms), no compute
  DMA, ring or locks; its shim supply can chain identical descriptors (repeat x chain records per task).
- constrain.request %poll, %tick: the poll fetches one record per tick through a shim lock (fresh reads, no run-ahead).
- constrain.gate %ch / constrain.signal %ch: the control program queues the core stream channels, waits for the gate
  before queueing anything else, and queues a signal's second record only after the invocation's other egress (done
  lands after the outputs). Streamed plans gain [gate | done] invocations (7 in all).
- Core stream plans zero every worker's private storage at array setup (tile memory keeps an earlier image's data).
- Router fix: a memory tile connects a north / south input only to the north / south output of the same channel
  (AIE-ML switch rule); routes through one now keep their channel (a mismatch lost a word per DMA transfer).
- Hard capacity checks in the program builder (release builds have no asserts).
Ungated images are byte-identical (the yah NPU GEMM image included).

